# Queer theory next to the love model: take the two sides out and count what breaks. See culture/queer/QUEER.md.
check "python3 -I culture/queer/roommates.py"
check "python3 -I culture/queer/traits.py"
frame "Gale and Shapley 1962 (College Admissions and the Stability of Marriage; a roommates instance with no stable matching) and Irving 1985 (an algorithm for it) (both cited from memory)" reading "checked-finite, roommates.py (the count only): with no sides, 0 of 1 profiles at n=2, 2 of 8 at n=3 and 48 of 1296 at n=4 have no stable matching; the smallest is three people ranking one another in a cycle. The two-sided model has a stable matching on all 46656 profiles at n=3 per side (culture/love/check.py). Checked: existence fails without sides. Not checked: that the sides caused the guarantee or stand for sex or gender; that link is an analogy, in the Butler frame" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 3 cost 40
frame "Fausto-Sterling, Sexing the Body (2000; cited from memory): sex as several traits" reading "checked-finite, traits.py: with k two-valued traits there are 2^k combinations and 2 are aligned; any one trait labels differently from another on 2^(k-1). On the grid of 1/4 steps (k <= 4) no threshold on one trait reproduces another. A toy count, not biology" -> 3 label checked-finite reach 3 cost 40
frame "Prevalence of intersex variation: Blackless et al. 2000 (about 1.7%, broad: any departure from the typical male or female body) and Sax 2002 (about 0.018%, narrow: chromosomal, gonadal or hormonal discordance only) (both cited from memory)" reading "open: the two figures are published and disagree. Sax argues it is which variations count; others dispute that. Nothing here chooses between them" -> none label open reach 2 cost 40
frame "Butler, Gender Trouble (1990; cited from memory): sex is constructed as gender, so sex/gender is not a categorical distinction" reading "ANALOGY (a reading): the love model's two sides are a binary built into the mathematics; dropping it is the roommates problem. The exact part is only that stability can then fail" -> none label open reach 3 cost 40
frame "Stryker, My Words to Victor Frankenstein (1994) and Transgender History (2008); Stone, The Empire Strikes Back: A Posttranssexual Manifesto (written 1987, published 1991) (all cited from memory)" reading "ANALOGY (a reading): trans people speaking in their own voice against a story written about them; this program does not model anyone's identity and asserts nothing about any person" -> none label open reach 2 cost 40
frame "Serano, Whipping Girl (2007; cited from memory): trans women, femininity and the way it is demeaned" reading "ANALOGY (a reading): a ranking that puts one side below the other is a preference profile with a built-in order; the model above ranks stated choices and cannot say who is good for anyone" -> none label open reach 2 cost 40
frame "Sedgwick, Epistemology of the Closet (1990; cited from memory): the hetero/homo binary organises much of modern knowledge" reading "ANALOGY (a reading): the same gesture as removing the sides; a binary assumed in the machinery, then asked of what happens without it" -> none label open reach 2 cost 40
frame "Beauvoir, The Second Sex (1949; cited from memory): reciprocity of the other" reading "OPEN: a model built on mutual recognition between people, not on two sides. The roommates model keeps reciprocity (a blocking pair needs both) and loses the guarantee; a new guarantee is not found here" -> none label open reach 3 cost 80
frame "Homestuck quadrants (culture/homestuck/quadrants/check.py): the four quadrant relations are not sexed" reading "ANALOGY (a reading): the trolls' relations name a kind of tie between any two, a signed graph with no sides. Roommates is the same shape for matching" -> none label open reach 2 cost 40
frame "Crenshaw 1989 (cited from memory) and culture/race: intersectionality margins" reading "ANALOGY (a reading): a joint table is not fixed by its margins (culture/race/race.py); several traits are not fixed by one label, the same fact in the cube. The count is in traits.py, the link is the reading" -> none label open reach 2 cost 40
record culture/queer queer checked-finite "queer.ath: with the two sides removed (roommates), 0 of 1, 2 of 8 and 48 of 1296 profiles (n = 2, 3, 4) have no stable matching, while the two-sided model has one on all 46656 n=3 profiles; with k two-valued traits 2^k - 2 combinations are not aligned, and on the 1/4 grid (k <= 4) no threshold on one trait reproduces another. Prevalence figures of 1.7% and 0.018% are published and not chosen between. The readings (Butler, Stryker, Stone, Serano, Sedgwick, Beauvoir) are analogy or open."
